[box=How to improve at osu!taiko (Crash Course Edition)]

[centre][i](This is just for the funsies so pls don't take it too seriously, criticize the maps but not the mappers ok thx)[/i][centre]


[list]
[*] Don't play converts. If you don't know what a convert is, stop reading this tutorial immediately (hehee :p)
[*] Use HT to learn new patterns.
[*] LEARN 1 OR 2 PATTERNS AT A TIME. TRYING TO GRASP TOO MANY NEW PATTERNS AT ONCE MIGHT OVERWHELM YOU.
[*] DON'T RETRY TOO OFTEN, DON'T PAUSE TOO OFTEN. TRY TO MOSTLY PLAY MAPS FROM BEGINNING TO END WITHOUT RETRYING OR PAUSING. They will kill your consistency.
[*] Use mods to improve your accuracy. Min-maxing OD adjustments from the editor works as well.
[*] Use edits (custom diffs where you crop the part of a map you're struggling with)
[*] Whenever you can't read a specific section in a map, memorization from the editor / muscle memory is your friend.
[*] Play a lot of "new" maps (i.e maps you haven't played yet)
[*] ^ Don't play a lot of "new" maps :p
[*] ^ ^ Basically, find the balance that works for you. For me, I prefer spending 2 - 5 full attempts per map. And no, you shouldn't play the same maps in many sessions in a row.
[*] PAUSE THE EDITOR, ZOOM IN OR OUT AS YOU NEED, AND LEARN PATTERNS FROM THERE BY TAPPING THEM ON YOUR DESK AT YOUR OWN PACE
[*] Don't play 3* Futsuu. Grow up and learn Muzukashii instead.
[*] Don't play 4* Muzukashii. Grow up and learn Oni instead.
[*] Don't play ranked maps. 99.99999% ranked maps are too easy. You won't get good playing 1* vocaloid songs.
[*] ^ [b] PLAYING TOURNAMENT MAPS AND GRAVEYARD MAPS IS LIKE THE ONLY WAY TO IMPROVE IN OSU!TAIKO. [/b]Some loveds are good too but some are not. When it comes to graveyard, try to seek "good mappers" (I don't know many, but like: kawaiibass, applerss, nananass, _Rise, hata no kokoro, _Kan2, Axer, etc.)
[*] ^ Don't play gimmick maps. Learning gimmick will only get you good at gimmick and nothing else, it's a skillset that is hard to leverage to other areas of the game.
[*] ^ Don't play Ono maps above 6*
[*] ^ Don't play super old (pre-2015) maps AT ALL
[*] ^ Play Nwolf maps, but only the ones within your skill range
[*] ^ Play some Nifty maps, but not too many.
[*] ^ Play every single NM1 and TB map out there.
[*] USE COLLECTION MANAGER
[*] USE OSU-TRAINER OR OSU!LAZER
[*] Learn kddk full alt [b](OPTIONAL)[/b]
[*] Use "legit" (≠ bannable) exploits [b](OPTIONAL)[/b]
[/list]

